      "id": "add-spectral-analysis-delegate",
      "name": "AddSpectralAnalysisDelegate",
      "category": "Audio",
      "signature": "AddSpectralAnalysisDelegate(Target, World Context Object, In Band Settings, On Submix Spectral Analysis BP, Update Rate, Decibel Noise Floor, Do Normalize, Do Auto Range, Auto Range Attack Time, Auto Range Release Time)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "USoundSubmix*"
        },
        {
          "name": "World Context Object",
          "type": "UObject*"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Band Settings",
          "type": "TArray<FSoundSubmixSpectralAnalysisBandSettings>&"
        },
        {
          "name": "On Submix Spectral Analysis BP",
          "type": "FOnSubmixSpectralAnalysisBP&"
        },
        {
          "name": "Update Rate",
          "type": "Float",
          "default": "10.f"
        },
        {
          "name": "Decibel Noise Floor",
          "type": "Float",
          "default": "-40.f"
        },
        {
          "name": "Do Normalize",
          "type": "Bool",
          "default": "true"
        },
        {
          "name": "Do Auto Range",
          "type": "Bool",
          "default": "false"
        },
        {
          "name": "Auto Range Attack Time",
          "type": "Float",
          "default": "0.1f"
        },
        {
          "name": "Auto Range Release Time",
          "type": "Float",
          "default": "60.f"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Void",
      "docs": "Adds a spectral analysis delegate to receive notifications when this submix has spectrum analysis enabled.\n@param\tInBandsettings\t\t\t\t\tThe frequency bands to analyze and their envelope-following settings.\n@param  OnSubmixSpectralAnalysisBP\t\tEvent to fire when new spectral data is available.\n@param\tUpdateRate\t\t\t\t\t\tHow often to retrieve the data from the spectral analyzer and broadcast the event. Max is 30 times per second.\n@param  InterpMethod                    Method to used for band peak calculation.\n@param  SpectrumType                    Metric to use when returning spectrum values.\n@param  DecibelNoiseFloor               Decibel Noise Floor to consider as silence when using a Decibel Spectrum Type.\n@param  bDoNormalize                    If true, output band values will be normalized between zero and one.\n@param  bDoAutoRange                    If true, output band values will have their ranges automatically adjusted to the minimum and maximum values in the audio. Output band values will be normalized between zero and one.\n@param  AutoRangeAttackTime             The time (in seconds) it takes for the range to expand to 90% of a larger range.\n@param  AutoRangeReleaseTime            The time (in seconds) it takes for the range to shrink to 90% of a smaller range."
    },
